Package: vault-rs
Version: 0.0.0-replaced-by-makefile
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: replaced-by-makefile
Recommends: openssl
Suggests: vault
Maintainer: Jérôme Poulin <jeromepoulin@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/ticpu/vault-rs
Description: PKI certificate management for HashiCorp Vault
 Issues, signs, inspects, verifies and exports certificates from a Vault PKI
 mount. Reads and writes paths, the KV engine, seal status and this session's
 token over the API itself, and forwards the verbs it does not model to the
 vault CLI with the server address and token already resolved. Output is one
 record per line for grep and awk, with an exit code that distinguishes an
 expiring certificate from a failure so cron and monitoring can act on it.
 Certificates and keys it issues are cached locally under a key held in the
 operator's own KV mount.
 .
 The vault CLI is needed only for the forwarded verbs, such as policy,
 operator and ssh; openssl only for --text output.
